4. Why not groupByKey(), aggregateByKey(), or combineByKey()?
========================================================================
groupByKey().mapValues(max)    same answer? True
aggregateByKey(no_scan, ...)   same answer? True
combineByKey(identity, f, f)   same answer? True

========================================================================
5. A common mistake: "the last one wins"
========================================================================
last_wins,  log order:      ('2026-10-20 19:40', 'Oakland, CA', 'in transit')
last_wins,  another order:  ('2026-10-21 06:05', 'Santa Clara, CA', 'out for delivery')
later_scan, log order:      ('2026-10-21 14:32', 'Santa Clara, CA', 'delivered')
later_scan, another order:  ('2026-10-21 14:32', 'Santa Clara, CA', 'delivered')

last_wins says 'in transit' (or 'out for delivery'), when the package
was delivered a day ago. later_scan compares the timestamps, so the
order doesn't matter.
